3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2 pattern (verbatim): `llm\\.overlap|enrich_drain|_read_llm_overlap_settings|_llm_drain_mode|DEFAULT_OVERLAP_|overlap_drain|digest_freshness|REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP` — none of these alternatives matches `overlap_verdict`, `overlap_verdict_batch`, `ticket_digest`, `OVERLAP_VERDICT`, `TICKET_DIGEST` (const), `overlap_judge`, or `*_response_model`.","src/rebar/llm/contracts.py:293 `register_contract(\"ticket_digest\", ticket_digest_response_model)`; :295 `register_contract(\"overlap_verdict\", overlap_verdict_response_model)`; :297 `register_contract(\"overlap_verdict_batch\", overlap_verdict_batch_response_model)`.","src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py:157 `OVERLAP_VERDICT = \"overlap_verdict\"`; :391 `\"enrich\": TICKET_DIGEST`; :394 `\"overlap_judge\": OVERLAP_VERDICT`.","tests/unit/test_run_request_builder.py:125,145,166,184 `output_schema=\"overlap_verdict\"` (5 occurrences); tests/unit/test_plan_review_overlap.py:23 and tests/unit/test_ticket_digest_store.py:19 `\"key_entities\": [\"review_plan\", \"overlap_verdict\"]`."],"finding":"AC2's completeness grep cannot match the removed contract/schema symbol family. The pattern `llm\\.overlap|enrich_drain|_read_llm_overlap_settings|_llm_drain_mode|DEFAULT_OVERLAP_|overlap_drain|digest_freshness|REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP` matches none of: contract factories `overlap_verdict_response_model`/`overlap_verdict_batch_response_model`/`ticket_digest_response_model` (contracts.py:150,175,201), their `register_contract(\"overlap_verdict\"|\"overlap_verdict_batch\"|\"ticket_digest\", ...)` calls (contracts.py:293,295,297), the schema constants `OVERLAP_VERDICT`/`TICKET_DIGEST` and `OUTPUT_SCHEMAS` synthetic keys `\"enrich\"`/`\"overlap_judge\"` (schemas/__init__.py:153,157,391,394). Live references to these names exist in files the summary does not individually name, so AC2 (the plan's stated completeness backstop) would report `nothing` while leftovers persist. The contract/schema inventory was evidently not derived from a symbol-reference lookup over these factory functions and schema constants.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe185ac6631eaa620","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC2 grep: `git grep -nE 'llm\\.overlap|enrich_drain|_read_llm_overlap_settings|_llm_drain_mode|DEFAULT_OVERLAP_|overlap_drain|digest_freshness|REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP'`; Scope 'Edit' naming contracts.py / schemas/__init__.py","norm_id":"na0e9c242053f1f6c","priority":0.6667,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["tests/unit/test_run_request_builder.py: five `output_schema=\"overlap_verdict\"` literals reference a now-deleted schema name; not matched by AC2 and not individually named, so a stale reference survives the completeness sweep.","src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py:391,394: the `OUTPUT_SCHEMAS` synthetic keys `\"enrich\"->TICKET_DIGEST` and `\"overlap_judge\"->OVERLAP_VERDICT` plus the `__all__` exports at :68,:81 — if the removal of these entries is skipped the schema-coverage guard still wires deleted schema files, breaking make verify after the .schema.json files are deleted.","src/rebar/llm/contracts.py:293-297: leftover `register_contract(\"overlap_verdict\"...)`/`register_contract(\"ticket_digest\"...)` would register models for deleted schemas and go unflagged by AC2.","src/rebar/llm/structured.py:114: comment naming `ticket_digest` as the exemplar 722-byte contract would dangle (prose, low risk, but illustrates the blind spot)."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add `overlap_verdict|overlap_verdict_batch|overlap_judge|_response_model|OVERLAP_VERDICT` to the AC2 pattern (and expect the retained event-name string `TICKET_DIGEST` to remain), run `find_referencing_symbols` on the three `*_response_model` factories and the `OVERLAP_VERDICT` constant, and name the resulting files (at minimum tests/unit/test_run_request_builder.py, tests/unit/test_plan_review_overlap.py, tests/unit/test_ticket_digest_store.py, src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py